            {
                "entry_id": "1e4beeef-fe7e-3781-b428-1dc27324bbbc",
                "word": "estaminet",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "96b73f45-d8f4-4719-ba6d-3aaab7fa5e32",
                        "entry_id": "1e4beeef-fe7e-3781-b428-1dc27324bbbc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "estaminets"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bb33c1f8-aad6-336c-9f5f-70386bfe73ef",
                        "entry_id": "1e4beeef-fe7e-3781-b428-1dc27324bbbc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Salle de café où l’on peut fumer en même temps que boire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9df60356-76bd-427e-86b9-cd23e3f94612",
                                "sense_id": "bb33c1f8-aad6-336c-9f5f-70386bfe73ef",
                                "text": "L’envoyé de Belzébuth s’adressa à un cercle de buveurs assis devant la porte de l’estaminet du Grand-Saint-Laurent, patron des verriers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d72fcb91-cbcb-41eb-a9fb-146894c41aa2",
                                "sense_id": "bb33c1f8-aad6-336c-9f5f-70386bfe73ef",
                                "text": "Et les buveurs qui fument dans l’estaminet borgne, et la servante de l’hôtellerie qui accroche à la fenêtre un faisan mort."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e4d79618-a8fa-484e-ab10-a6f5c8e56619",
                                "sense_id": "bb33c1f8-aad6-336c-9f5f-70386bfe73ef",
                                "text": "Il ne pouvait suivre aucune carrière, étant absorbé dans les estaminets."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8e632f83-701c-366b-85ad-55d8839718d3",
                        "entry_id": "1e4beeef-fe7e-3781-b428-1dc27324bbbc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Petit café restaurant fréquenté par une clientèle populaire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Nord-Pas-de-Calais",
                            "Belgique",
                            "Aujourd’hui"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d2b74c8-1e5a-4768-bcce-aca8a414374d",
                                "sense_id": "8e632f83-701c-366b-85ad-55d8839718d3",
                                "text": "Estaminets, brasseries, bar-tabacs, chacun avait son charme. Si je savais rester en retrait, à bonne fortune de bar, je n'étais jamais le dernier à requérir l'assistance du maître des lieux."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bad5c3da-8dc9-4506-a8b6-be83744add45",
                                "sense_id": "8e632f83-701c-366b-85ad-55d8839718d3",
                                "text": "Bien acagnardé contre le zinc à pampres de son estaminet de prédilection, Antonin lantiponait à foison parmi des norias de pieds nickelés en mouillage. Il retrouvait en ces lieux surchauffés des gens de toutes conditions, de toutes extractions […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "94d503a1-8491-4aaf-934d-d9865c3b4c68",
                        "source_entry_id": "1e4beeef-fe7e-3781-b428-1dc27324bbbc",
                        "target_lang_word": "tavern",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tavern",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d908740a-0dae-3114-899f-66fff910f105",
                                        "entry_id": "b7c1f76c-1c6f-3139-86d7-e6560696fb73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A restaurant or bar."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52a8afc9-48a4-37e1-a5b8-c334cc0e19ce",
                                        "entry_id": "b7c1f76c-1c6f-3139-86d7-e6560696fb73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A building containing a bar licensed to sell alcoholic drinks, and offering sleeping accommodations for travelers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a43f2f1e-4abf-44fb-8631-8bb4ebd4726a",
                                                "sense_id": "52a8afc9-48a4-37e1-a5b8-c334cc0e19ce",
                                                "text": "I maruell I heare no nevves of Dromio, either hee ſlackes the matter, or betraies his Maiſter, I dare not motion anie thing to Stellio, till I knovv vvhat my boy hath don, Ile hunt him out, if the loiterſacke be gone ſpringing into a Tauerne, Ile fetch him reeling out."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c328dc87-cacf-4c41-b96f-91e021262f3f",
                                                "sense_id": "52a8afc9-48a4-37e1-a5b8-c334cc0e19ce",
                                                "text": "Dreaming when Dawn's Left Hand was in the Sky / I heard a Voice within the Tavern cry, / \"Awake, my Little ones, and fill the Cup / Before Life's Liquor in its Cup be dry.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d37e62d6-f9bb-40e2-b97e-b78a45bf16ad",
                                                "sense_id": "52a8afc9-48a4-37e1-a5b8-c334cc0e19ce",
                                                "text": "At half-past nine on this Saturday evening the parlor of the Salutation Inn, High Holborn, contained most of its customary visitors. […] In former days every tavern of repute kept such a room for the select circle—a club, or society, of habitués, who met every evening for a pipe and a cheerful glass."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3ad9408-028d-4f08-8277-53b7d75b8e5b",
                                                "sense_id": "52a8afc9-48a4-37e1-a5b8-c334cc0e19ce",
                                                "text": "At one of the way-stations on his long journey a barmaid at a tavern speaks to Gilgamesh and tries to give him common sense on the human condition."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a52bd6d4-66ef-4e6c-b910-ddfefa0a8451",
                        "source_entry_id": "1e4beeef-fe7e-3781-b428-1dc27324bbbc",
